<.shell title="Tag" current={:tag}>
  <h1>Tag</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A word or two of status. Tinted tags say what something is. Solid tags ask for action.
  </p>

  <div class="demo">
    <p class="paragraph">
      In a table row: Casey Dhillon, Wilderness First Aid
      <.badge kind={:warning}>12 days</.badge>
    </p>
    <p class="paragraph">
      Beside a heading: Missing hiker, Stawamus Chief
      <.badge kind={:incident}>Incident</.badge>
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Kinds</h2>
  <p>
    Five status tags, the three D4H activity kinds as a tag or a marker, and an outlined tag for D4H's own tags.
  </p>
  <.table id="tag-kinds" rows={tag_kinds()}>
    <:col :let={t} label="Tag" class="whitespace-nowrap">
      <span :if={t.kind == :kinds} class="badges">
        <.badge kind={:incident}>Incident</.badge>
        <.badge kind={:exercise}>Exercise</.badge>
        <.badge kind={:event}>Event</.badge>
      </span>
      <span :if={t.kind == :markers} class="badges">
        <.activity_kind activity={
          %{activity_kind: "incident", is_published: true, tracking_number: nil}
        } />
        <.activity_kind activity={
          %{activity_kind: "exercise", is_published: true, tracking_number: nil}
        } />
        <.activity_kind activity={
          %{activity_kind: "event", is_published: true, tracking_number: nil}
        } />
      </span>
      <.badge :if={t.kind not in [:kinds, :markers]} kind={t.kind}>{t.sample}</.badge>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={t} label="Look" class="w-px whitespace-nowrap">{t.look}</:col>
    <:col :let={t} label="Means">{t.means}</:col>
    <:col :let={t} label="Examples">{t.examples}</:col>
  </.table>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A state people scan for in a list, such as Expired or Draft.</li>
    <li>The kind of an activity, beside its title or in a table column.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A normal state gets no tag. Show "Draft" on an unpublished activity, never "Published" on the rest.
    </li>
    <li>Codes such as tracking numbers are mono text, not tags.</li>
    <li>Tags are labels, not buttons. Nothing happens when you select one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>One to three words. The words carry the meaning; the colour helps people scan.</li>
    <li>At most one status tag per row or item. If two apply, show the more urgent one.</li>
    <li>
      Amber and red are for things a person should act on. If everything is amber, nothing is.
    </li>
    <li>
      A column where every row has a tag is too loud. Show the D4H kind there as a marker, and
      fold D4H's primary and secondary hours tags into the Hours column as a word.
    </li>
    <li>
      Several tags together sit in a <code>.badges</code>
      group, so they wrap with a gap and never touch.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.badge kind=&#123;:warning&#125;&gt;</code>, and
    <code>&lt;.activity_kind activity=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    for the marker. The kind is checked when the app compiles.
  </p>
</.shell>
